---

<Base title="About" description="What OwnPulse is, why it exists, and how the cooperative model works.">
  <!-- Mission -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20 bg-surface-elevated">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-neutral-900 font-display">Health is personal. Your tools should be too.</h1>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Mainstream health apps are built for the average person. They track steps and sleep and
          call it a day. But if you're running a peptide protocol, dialing in a supplement stack,
          tracking how meetings affect your HRV, or trying to correlate glucose with mood — you're
          on your own, stitching together data from a dozen apps that were never designed to talk
          to each other.
        </p>
        <p>
          OwnPulse is built for people who take health optimization seriously. It brings your
          signals onto a single timeline — Apple Health data, manual labs, interventions,
          subjective check-ins, and observations — so you can see the full picture and run your
          own analysis. No one else decides what's worth tracking. No substance name gets flagged
          or filtered.
        </p>
        <p>
          The app is open for review and self-hosting. The hosted service is the convenience layer:
          storage, backups, monitoring, upgrades, and operations for people who do not want to run
          their own server.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What OwnPulse tracks -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20 bg-surface">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-900 font-display">What OwnPulse tracks</h2>

      <div class="mt-10 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-800">Wearables &amp; devices</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-600">
            HRV, resting heart rate, sleep, steps, weight, and other supported Apple HealthKit
            measurements. Additional wearable and CGM integrations are roadmap items.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-800">Interventions</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-600">
            Medications, supplements, peptides, nootropics — substance, dose, unit, route, timing,
            fasted state. The platform is non-judgmental: if you're taking it, it's valid data.
            Log BPC-157, metformin, or lion's mane the same way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-800">Subjective check-ins</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-600">
            Five daily scores (1-10): energy, mood, focus, recovery, libido. Takes less than 30
            seconds. Over time, these correlate with objective metrics in ways that surprise you.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-800">Labs</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-600">
            Blood panel data with reference ranges entered manually. Lab PDF parsing is planned,
            but V1 keeps the data model explicit and exportable.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-800">Calendar &amp; lifestyle</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-600">
            Meeting count and minutes per day are planned as lifestyle signals. Meeting load is
            health data, but it should be connected only when you explicitly choose to connect it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-800">Everything else</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-600">
            Cold plunge, sauna, fasting windows, pain scales, symptoms, travel, altitude, air quality,
            freeform notes. If it affects your health, you can track it — no waiting for us to add
            support.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Community and sharing -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20 bg-surface-elevated">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-900 font-display">Open source, paid operations</h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          OwnPulse's application code is public so privacy claims can be checked. The paid product
          is managed hosting and storage: keeping the service online, upgraded, backed up, monitored,
          and recoverable.
        </p>
        <p>
          Self-hosters can run the same application on their own infrastructure. Hosted users pay
          for convenience and reliability, not for a proprietary version of their own health data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cooperative aggregate learning is a future opt-in capability. It is not required for V1
          and it is never a default data-sharing behavior.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Your data, your control -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20 bg-surface">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-900 font-display">Your data, your control</h2>

      <ul class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-lg text-neutral-600">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent font-bold shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
          <span>Full export anytime — JSON and CSV in V1, with FHIR R4 planned. No artificial delay.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent font-bold shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
          <span>Data sharing is opt-in, per dataset, revocable immediately. Nothing is shared by default.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent font-bold shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
          <span>No analytics, no telemetry, no phone-home behavior in the application.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent font-bold shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
          <span>Open source — you can read every line of code that touches your data.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-accent font-bold shrink-0">&mdash;</span>
          <span>Want full control? <a href="https://github.com/ownpulse/ownpulse/blob/main/docs/guides/self-hosting.md" class="text-primary hover:text-primary-dark underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Self-host on your own server.</a></span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Team / founding -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20 bg-surface-elevated">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-900 font-display">Who's building this</h2>

      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
        OwnPulse is early stage. Built by people who track peptides, supplements, and biomarkers
        — and got frustrated that no platform treats all of that as legitimate data in one place.
        We wanted a tool that lets us overlay every health signal on a single timeline, run our
        own correlations, and decide for ourselves what matters.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
        If that sounds like you, <a href="#waitlist" class="text-primary hover:text-primary-dark underline">join the waitlist</a>
        or <a href="https://github.com/ownpulse/ownpulse" class="text-primary hover:text-primary-dark underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">contribute on GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
